# Database Rules — Pocket Portfolio

## Schema Conventions
- Table names: lowercase snake_case, plural (e.g., `holdings`, `accounts`, `audit_logs`)
- Column names: lowercase snake_case (e.g., `cost_basis_cents`, `created_at`)
- Primary keys: UUID v4 generated by PostgreSQL (`gen_random_uuid()`)
- Foreign keys: always reference the `id` column of the parent table
- Timestamps: `created_at` and `updated_at` on EVERY table, with `updated_at` auto-updating via trigger
- Soft deletes: use `deleted_at` timestamp (nullable) instead of hard deletes on financial data
- Money columns: `bigint` type, column name suffixed with `_cents` (e.g., `cost_basis_cents`, `market_value_cents`)

## Drizzle Schema Pattern
```tsx
// src/db/schema/holdings.ts
import { pgTable, uuid, text, bigint, integer, timestamp, pgEnum } from "drizzle-orm/pg-core";

export const assetTypeEnum = pgEnum("asset_type", [
  "stock", "etf", "mutual_fund", "bond", "crypto",
  "real_estate", "cash", "other"
]);

export const holdings = pgTable("holdings", {
  id: uuid("id").defaultRandom().primaryKey(),
  userId: text("user_id").notNull(), // Clerk user ID
  accountId: uuid("account_id").notNull().references(() => accounts.id),
  ticker: text("ticker"), // Null for non-market assets like real estate
  name: text("name").notNull(),
  assetType: assetTypeEnum("asset_type").notNull(),
  shares: integer("shares"), // Null for real estate, cash
  costBasisCents: bigint("cost_basis_cents", { mode: "number" }).notNull(),
  acquiredAt: timestamp("acquired_at", { withTimezone: true }),
  notes: text("notes"),
  isLiquidated: boolean("is_liquidated").default(false),
  liquidatedAt: timestamp("liquidated_at", { withTimezone: true }),
  createdAt: timestamp("created_at", { withTimezone: true }).defaultNow().notNull(),
  updatedAt: timestamp("updated_at", { withTimezone: true }).defaultNow().notNull(),
  deletedAt: timestamp("deleted_at", { withTimezone: true }),
});
```

## RLS Policy Patterns
ALWAYS create RLS policies per operation (never use FOR ALL). Read `docs/security.md` before writing policies.

```sql
-- Enable RLS on table
ALTER TABLE holdings ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;

-- Users can only see their own holdings
CREATE POLICY "users_select_own_holdings" ON holdings
  FOR SELECT USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Users can only insert their own holdings  
CREATE POLICY "users_insert_own_holdings" ON holdings
  FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Users can only update their own holdings
CREATE POLICY "users_update_own_holdings" ON holdings
  FOR UPDATE USING (auth.uid() = user_id)
  WITH CHECK (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Users can only soft-delete their own holdings
CREATE POLICY "users_delete_own_holdings" ON holdings
  FOR DELETE USING (auth.uid() = user_id);

-- Wealth managers can view assigned client holdings
CREATE POLICY "wm_select_client_holdings" ON holdings
  FOR SELECT USING (
    EXISTS (
      SELECT 1 FROM client_assignments
      WHERE client_assignments.wealth_manager_id = auth.uid()
      AND client_assignments.client_id = holdings.user_id
    )
  );

-- Admins can view all holdings
CREATE POLICY "admin_select_all_holdings" ON holdings
  FOR SELECT USING (
    (auth.jwt() -> 'metadata' ->> 'role') = 'admin'
  );
```

## Index Requirements
- Index ALL columns used in RLS policies (`user_id` on every table)
- Index foreign key columns
- Composite index on `(user_id, account_id)` for holdings lookups
- Composite index on `(user_id, ticker)` for cross-custodian grouping
- Index `created_at` on audit_logs for time-range queries

## Migration Rules
- Never modify existing migration files — always create new ones
- Test migrations against a staging Supabase project before production
- Include both `up` and `down` migrations
- Data migrations (backfills) go in separate files from schema migrations

## Audit Log Table
The audit_logs table is append-only. RLS allows INSERT for authenticated users, SELECT for admins only. No UPDATE or DELETE policies ever.

```sql
CREATE TABLE audit_logs (
  id UUID DEFAULT gen_random_uuid() PRIMARY KEY,
  actor_id TEXT NOT NULL,
  action TEXT NOT NULL CHECK (action IN ('CREATE', 'UPDATE', 'DELETE', 'LOGIN', 'EXPORT', 'ROLE_CHANGE')),
  resource_type TEXT NOT NULL,
  resource_id UUID,
  metadata JSONB DEFAULT '{}',
  ip_address INET,
  success BOOLEAN DEFAULT true,
  created_at TIMESTAMPTZ DEFAULT NOW() NOT NULL
);

-- Append-only: users can insert, admins can read, nobody can modify
ALTER TABLE audit_logs ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;
CREATE POLICY "insert_audit" ON audit_logs FOR INSERT WITH CHECK (true);
CREATE POLICY "admin_read_audit" ON audit_logs FOR SELECT USING (
  (auth.jwt() -> 'metadata' ->> 'role') = 'admin'
);
```
